{"invalidate_upsampling_cache computes the cache key using Python's hash(), which is randomized per-process since Python 3.3. When called from a different process than the one that set the cache, the hash value differs and the cache deletion silently fails to target the correct entry. Should use a stable hash like hashlib.sha256 or sorting and joining the project IDs.": 0.9631496667861938, "In _get_event_stats, the upsampling eligibility check at line 220-221 uses dataset (the outer closure variable) instead of scoped_dataset (the function parameter). When _get_event_stats is called with different datasets, the upsampling check evaluates against the original dataset rather than the actual dataset being queried, causing incorrect upsampling decisions.": 0.9474756121635437}